---
import CopyCommand from "../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const INSTALL = "curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danieldunderfelt/baton/main/install.sh | sh";
const REGISTER = "baton install --user";

const apps = ["Claude Code", "Codex", "Kimi Code", "OpenCode", "Cursor Agent"];

const features = [
  {
    title: "Delegate through MCP",
    body: "Any app that speaks MCP can call run_model and get an answer from a model running in another app. The callee shares the filesystem, nothing else.",
    href: "/docs/delegating",
  },
  {
    title: "Routing on evidence",
    body: "Grade what comes back. Grades decay with a 90-day half-life, seeded opinions are capped, and blind duels feed a Bradley-Terry score. Baton picks routes on what you observed.",
    href: "/docs/ratings",
  },
  {
    title: "Two subscriptions, one pool",
    body: "Two accounts for the same app become one bigger one. Selection favours quota headroom, rate limits trigger cooldown and failover, and nothing re-runs after work may have started.",
    href: "/docs/load-balancing",
  },
  {
    title: "Rails, not hope",
    body: "Delegation depth is capped, every app has an autonomy ceiling, retries are idempotent, and a timeout kills the whole process tree and checks that it is dead.",
    href: "/docs/delegating",
  },
  {
    title: "Routes you can refuse",
    body: "Block a client's seat or a provider with one pattern. A blocked route is never chosen, not even as a last resort, and every scope only knows its own accounts.",
    href: "/docs/blocking",
  },
  {
    title: "Profiles that travel",
    body: "Your opinion of each model is a profile: canonical priors and nothing local. Share it with a code, import someone else's, and see the diff before anything is written.",
    href: "/docs/sharing",
  },
];
---

<Base title="Baton">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">For coding agents on your own machine</p>
      <h1>Hand work to any model, from any agent.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Baton lets the coding agent you are talking to pass a task to a model running in a <em>different</em> agent app on the same machine, on that app's own subscription. Claude
        Code asks Codex for a review. Codex pushes a migration to Kimi. Every run is recorded,
        graded, and used to route the next one.
      </p>
      <div class="install stack">
        <CopyCommand command={INSTALL} />
        <CopyCommand command={REGISTER} />
        <p class="muted small">
          macOS or Linux, arm64 or x64. The first line installs a checksum-verified binary into <code>~/.local/bin</code>. The second registers Baton with every supported agent app on
          your PATH. <a href="/docs/installation">Installation details</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="terminal" aria-label="Example: delegating from an agent session">
        <div class="terminal-bar">
          <span></span><span></span><span></span>
          <p>Claude Code · a session with Baton installed</p>
        </div>
        <pre><code><span class="t-user">›</span> <span class="t-bold">Have Codex review this diff for anything that could lose data.</span>

<span class="t-dim">⏺</span> baton · run_model <span class="t-dim">(model: gpt-5.6-sol, category: review)</span>
  <span class="t-dim">→ codex exec … on subscription "work"  ·  14.2s</span>

<span class="t-dim">⏺</span> Two findings came back. The second one is real: the migration
  drops the column before the backfill commits. I've reordered the
  steps and added a rollback guard.

<span class="t-dim">⏺</span> baton · report_result <span class="t-dim">(grade: 4, "caught the ordering bug; one false positive")</span></code></pre>
      </div>
      <ul class="apps row" aria-label="Supported agent apps">
        <li class="faint">Runs models through</li>
        {apps.map((app) => <li class="pill">{app}</li>)}
        <li class="faint">and any app you teach it</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="how">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>One binary, two faces</h2>
      <div class="steps">
        <div>
          <span class="n">1</span>
          <h3>Agents call in over MCP</h3>
          <p>
            <code>baton mcp</code> is an MCP server. Any app that can use tools can delegate with <code>run_model</code>, poll long runs, or resume a finished one in the callee's own session.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="n">2</span>
          <h3>Baton drives the other app's CLI</h3>
          <p>
            It picks a route for the requested model, spawns that app's command line with the
            environment it inherited, and captures the answer. No API proxy, so your existing
            subscriptions are what run the work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="n">3</span>
          <h3>Results become evidence</h3>
          <p>
            Every run lands in SQLite. Grade it after using it, and the rating of that model for
            that kind of task moves. The next delegation routes on what actually happened.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid">
        {
          features.map((f) => (
            <a class="feature card" href={f.href}>
              <h3>{f.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{f.body}</p>
              <span class="more">Read more</span>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="honest">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>What it deliberately does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            It does not verify identity. Baton runs each CLI with the environment it inherited,
            exactly as if you had typed the command. Separate your worlds with <code>BATON_CONFIG_DIR</code> and direnv.
          </li>
          <li>
            It does not sandbox callees beyond what each CLI's own autonomy flags offer. You set
            the ceiling per app.
          </li>
          <li>
            It does not send prompts anywhere. They stay in a capped local ring buffer. Only
            aggregate ratings are shareable.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 5.5rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, 3.75rem);
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    max-width: 16ch;
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .lede {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .lede em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .install {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
    --gap: 0.6rem;
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .small a {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .demo {
    padding: 2rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .terminal {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-code);
    color: var(--fg-code);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .terminal-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.08);
  }
  .terminal-bar span {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.15);
  }
  .terminal-bar p {
    margin-left: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #8a8a94;
  }
  .terminal pre {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .t-user {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .t-bold {
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .t-dim {
    color: #7c7c86;
  }
  .apps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    --gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .how {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .how h2,
  .honest h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }
  .steps h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .n {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .features {
    padding: 1rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .feature {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    transition: border-color 120ms ease, transform 120ms ease;
  }
  .feature:hover {
    color: inherit;
    border-color: var(--line-strong);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .feature h3 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .feature p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .more {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .honest {
    padding: 0 0 5rem;
  }
  .honest .card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
  }
  .honest ul {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .honest li + li {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
</style>
